al Working at RWTH Working in RWTH’s Scientific Community Working in Management, Administration, Technology & IT Career & Personal Development RWTH Welcome Center Interesting Facts Living in Aachen and Beyond Sustainability Submenu: Sustainability Sustainability Strategy Sustainability Report Sustainability Mission Statement Sustainability Focus Areas Networks Help Build a Sustainable RWTH Newsletter, FAQ and Downloads Faculties Submenu: Faculties Faculty 1 Mathematics and Natural Sciences Faculty 2 Architecture Faculty 3 Civil Engineering Faculty 4 Mechanical Engineering Faculty 5 Georesources and Materials Engineering Faculty 6 Electrical Engineering and Information Technology Faculty 7 Arts and Humanities Faculty 8 Business and Economics Faculty 9 Computer Science Faculty 10 Medicine Information for... Quick Access Prospective Students First Year Students Students Early-Career Researchers Researchers International Alumni School Students Corporate Visitors Press Tools RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle Intranet Services Dining Hall Menus RWTH Navigator Student Resources and Support Official Announcements Institutions University Library IT Center Center for Teaching and Learning Services Athletics and Recreation Central University Administration Search by Name Search for Search You Are Here: Start Academics After Graduation Career Center Career Center Connecting With Companies Job Openings for RWTH Graduates Application Tips Application Advice Competitions and Recruiting Events Events to Help Prepare You to Start Your Career Female Careers Career for Graduates Copyright: © Andreas Steindl The Career Center is your gateway to professional success, providing the tools, resources, and connections you need to launch your career with confidence. We bring together RWTH’s full range of career services in one central location, serving as a dynamic link between talented students and forward-thinking employers. Contact Anja Robert M.A. Relationship Management Staff Unit Career Center Coordinator, Career and Application Advising, Contact for Companies and Collaborations Work Phone:  + 4 9 2 4 1 8 0 9 9 1 2 2 +49 241 80-99122 Work Send Email Seminars & Career Training The Career Center will help you start your career by providing opportunities to strengthen your professionalism and boost your career skills. Each semester, we put together a comprehensive program of seminars and career training sessions to help you get started in your career. As a rule, our events take place online. You can find more details in the event overview . Finding and Meeting Companies On our Finding Companies web page, we have listed the different ways you can find and meet companies. Firms looking for RWTH graduates present themselves to students in various formats. It is easy to get to know potential employers and establish initial contact with them. Femtec Career Building Program Femtec.Network is a joint career program developed by eleven large enterprises, which aims to prepare women from engineering and the natural sciences from the eight participating universities for management positions. Our Career Services for Internationals team is dedicated to helping international students and graduates realize their career objectives. We offer tailored advice, engaging workshops, and valuable networking opportunities to ease your entry into the German job market. Job Banks & Bulletin Boards Our job board highlights opportunities from companies specifically seeking LTE graduates and students. Additionally, these and other job announcements are posted on our bulletin board in the foyer of the C.A.R.L. lecture hall complex. Application Tips If you need to apply to a position quickly, take a look at our application tips . Here, you will find everything you need for a successful application process. Personal Advising on Application Processes and Portfolio Reviews The Career Center team offers all RWTH students, doctoral candidates, and postdocs the opportunity to have their job application portfolios reviewed . If you need an application portfolio review for materials in English, we will gladly provide you with contact information for external services with whom we have worked successfully for many years. RWTH Careers Portal As the largest employer in the Aachen region, RWTH offers a wide range of entry-level and professional development opportunities. Whether you are interested in research or roles in management, administration, technology, or IT, the RWTH Careers Portal helps you explore career paths and plan your next steps at the University. Similar Topics Preparing for Your Career Extracurricular & Leisure Activities Here you will find associations, initiatives, and organizations where you can volunteer or gain practical experience. International Opportunities Interesting information about studies or internships abroad Femtec.Network Support for Female Students in the Engineering and Natural Sciences Skills Training for Doctoral Candidates at the Doctoral Academy Division 12.1 - Early-Career Researcher Development and Talent Management Support for scientific staff TANDEM Mentoring Programs Mentoring, training, and networking services for researchers and junior researchers at various points in their careers and with different qualifications Founding a Start-Up Health Campaigns Here you will find offers from student health management Footer Services Contact and Directions Legal Notice Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement Site Map Safety Feedback Glossary of Academic Terms Other Portals RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle RWTH Jobs Portal University Library Athletics and Recreation Intranet RWTH in Simple English Further Institutions © 2026 RWTH Aachen University Social Media Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Facebook Threads BlueSky Mastodon RWTH Social Media"
    },
