H Jobs Portal Working at RWTH Working in RWTH’s Scientific Community Working in Management, Administration, Technology & IT Career & Personal Development RWTH Welcome Center Interesting Facts Living in Aachen and Beyond Sustainability Submenu: Sustainability Sustainability Strategy Sustainability Report Sustainability Mission Statement Sustainability Focus Areas Networks Help Build a Sustainable RWTH Newsletter, FAQ and Downloads Faculties Submenu: Faculties Faculty 1 Mathematics and Natural Sciences Faculty 2 Architecture Faculty 3 Civil Engineering Faculty 4 Mechanical Engineering Faculty 5 Georesources and Materials Engineering Faculty 6 Electrical Engineering and Information Technology Faculty 7 Arts and Humanities Faculty 8 Business and Economics Faculty 9 Computer Science Faculty 10 Medicine Information for... Quick Access Prospective Students First Year Students Students Early-Career Researchers Researchers International Alumni School Students Corporate Visitors Press Tools RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle Intranet Services Dining Hall Menus RWTH Navigator Student Resources and Support Official Announcements Institutions University Library IT Center Center for Teaching and Learning Services Athletics and Recreation Central University Administration Search by Name Search for Search You Are Here: Start Research Services for Researchers Qualification and Career Qualification and Career RWTH Center for Young Academics Copyright: © Martin Braun Academic careers are as diverse as they are demanding, requiring not only excellent qualifications but also strong support systems. RWTH provides both, offering development programs that build on individual strengths while creating the structures researchers need to thrive. RWTH Aachen University offers doctoral candidates, postdocs, professors, mid-level academic staff, and academic administrators a comprehensive range of training programs to develop their careers and leadership skills. To provide tailored support to different target groups, RWTH has a system of specialized centers. These centers are closely networked and they provide support for academic careers as well as for positions of responsibility in technology and administration. Center for Young Academics The Center for Young Academics , or CYA for short, is the central point of contact for information, career development, and networking for doctoral candidates, postdocs, and advanced talents at RWTH. Here, we closely advise and support early-career researchers along their career path , from the doctoral stage to the postdoc period through to the professorship. The RWTH Doctoral Academy – formerly known as the Center for Doctoral Studies, CDS – offers doctoral candidates a wide range of transversal skills development courses as well as coaching and advising for systematic career planning. The RWTH Postdoc Academy is the central point of contact for you if you have completed your doctorate and are now in your postdoc phase. We support you in achieving scientific excellence and independence, making important career decisions, networking with other postdocs, and gaining targeted interdisciplinary qualification. Copyright: © Martin Braun Center for Professional Leadership, CPL The Center for Professional Leadership , CPL, is a central point of contact that supports staff in sustainably developing their leadership competencies. We also promote open, inspiring networking among your peers and work on individual issues with you. You are bound to find an offer that appeals to you from our portfolio of workshops, individual coaching, and inspiring and networking events. Copyright: © Martin Braun Center for Staff Development, CSD At the Center for Staff Development , CSD, postdocs and science managers can professionalize their key competencies in a wide range of subject-specific and interdisciplinary areas. Together with technical and administrative employees, you will benefit from our wide range of workshops, counseling, individual coaching, networking, and exchange formats, as well as support for department-specific needs. Copyright: © Martin Braun Similar Topics Careers for Researchers Career Advising for Academic Staff at RWTH Leadership at RWTH Third Party Funding Staff Development at RWTH RWTH Jobs Portal Footer Services Contact and Directions Legal Notice Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement Site Map Safety Feedback Glossary of Academic Terms Other Portals RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle RWTH Jobs Portal University Library Athletics and Recreation Intranet RWTH in Simple English Further Institutions © 2026 RWTH Aachen University Social Media Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Facebook Threads BlueSky Mastodon RWTH Social Media"
    },
