 Property What Is Intellectual Property? IP Consulting Disclosing an Invention or Software Invention Patent and Standards Center Partnerships and Collaborations Submenu: Partnerships and Collaborations Collaboration Opportunities for Companies Technology Commercialization at RWTH Partnering With RWTH Startups Continuing Education Programs of RWTH International Academy Research Campus Submenu: Research Campus Where Science Meets Industry Campus Melaten Campus West Recruiting Submenu: Recruiting Connect with RWTH’s Top Talent Career Days and Fairs Company Presentations Dean’s List – Opportunities for Companies Employer Branding and Year-Round Visibility Advertise Job Opportunities Further Collaboration Opportunities Giving and Sponsorship Submenu: Giving and Sponsorship Giving Sponsorship Endowments Deutschlandstipendium Scholarship Program About RWTH Submenu: About RWTH Profile Submenu: Profile Our Identity Facts, Figures and Rankings: RWTH in Overview Principles and Strategy Internationalization Entrepreneurial University Awards and Honors Voluntary Leadership in Research History of RWTH Aachen University Excellence Strategy Submenu: Excellence Strategy The Excellence Strategy at RWTH University of Excellence Clusters of Excellence at RWTH Institutional Strategy II Institutional Strategy I Academic and Administrative Units Submenu: Academic and Administrative Units Faculties Rectorate Organizational Structure University Administration Campus Resources Central Institutions Staff Councils & Other Representations Featured RWTH Events Submenu: Featured RWTH Events Science Events for the Public RWTHextern – University for Everyone Honors Awarded to Our Graduates and Early-Career Researchers Honors Awarded by RWTH and the City of Aachen Special Honors Awarded by RWTH Special RWTH Events The RWTH Community Submenu: The RWTH Community Gender and Diversity Inclusion and Accessibility Family-Friendly University and Work Life Balance Health Portal Career Submenu: Career RWTH Jobs Portal Working at RWTH Working in RWTH’s Scientific Community Working in Management, Administration, Technology & IT Career & Personal Development RWTH Welcome Center Interesting Facts Living in Aachen and Beyond Sustainability Submenu: Sustainability Sustainability Strategy Sustainability Report Sustainability Mission Statement Sustainability Focus Areas Networks Help Build a Sustainable RWTH Newsletter, FAQ and Downloads Faculties Submenu: Faculties Faculty 1 Mathematics and Natural Sciences Faculty 2 Architecture Faculty 3 Civil Engineering Faculty 4 Mechanical Engineering Faculty 5 Georesources and Materials Engineering Faculty 6 Electrical Engineering and Information Technology Faculty 7 Arts and Humanities Faculty 8 Business and Economics Faculty 9 Computer Science Faculty 10 Medicine Information for... Quick Access Prospective Students First Year Students Students Early-Career Researchers Researchers International Alumni School Students Corporate Visitors Press Tools RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle Intranet Services Dining Hall Menus RWTH Navigator Student Resources and Support Official Announcements Institutions University Library IT Center Center for Teaching and Learning Services Athletics and Recreation Central University Administration Search by Name Search for Search You Are Here: Start Transfer Recruiting Career Days and Fairs Career Days and Fairs Strategic Networking for Targeted Talent Copyright: © Stefan Hense Contact Diana Küpper Event Management Work Phone:  + 4 9 2 4 1 8 0 9 2 7 2 4 +49 241 80-92724 Work Send Email In-Person and Digital Career Days Our Career Day series provides a premier platform for organizations—ranging from innovative startups to global corporations—to showcase their brand to a diverse student body. These focused recruitment fairs allow companies to connect with high-potential students who are still exploring their career paths. Whether on-site or in a virtual space, our Career Days make it easy to network with RWTH graduates and secure your future workforce. The participation fee for each event is €1,300. Detailed information regarding event packages and schedules can be found below. The following dates and topics are planned for the 2026/27 winter semester: Career Day – Consulting (In Person) on October 19, 2026, 3 to 6pm If you represent a consulting firm that is interested in connecting with RWTH students and doctoral candidates, we’d  encourage you to join us for Career Day – Consulting. Career Day – The Future of Energy (In Person) on November 17, 2026, 3 to 6pm Does your company deal with energy-related matters or does it operate in the energy sector? Have you set a goal to review and restructure your production, processes, or operations with a view to improve sustainability? If so, take advantage of this event to introduce your company to RWTH students and graduates who want to use their knowledge to shape a sustainable future. Digital Career Day – KI and Digitalization (Online), on December 2, 2026, 5 to 7pm If you’d like to introduce your company to tech-savvy students who are interested in the latest developments in AI and digital transformation, we look forward to seeing you at this Career Day. Career Day – Direct Entry and Traineeships (In Person) on December 17, 2026, 3 to 6pm Are you looking for top students or recent graduates in STEM subjects, engineering, and business for your trainee positions or to join your company directly? If so, this is the right event for you. Career Day – Mobility (In Person) on January 11, 2027, 3 to 6pm Whether it’s electric mobility, autonomous driving, or connected mobility—if you’re developing concepts and products for the mobility of tomorrow and are looking for young talent to help you advance these areas, you’ll find what you’re looking for at this event. Career Day for Women (In Person) on January 20, 2027, 3 to 6pm If your company is specifically looking to hire female students and doctoral candidates, then this Career Day for Women is the event you need. In-Person Career Days Our in-person career fairs, hosting up to 20 organizations, are held in a centrally located building on the RWTH campus from 3 to 6pm. This format allows your team to engage with up to 180 students at dedicated information booths and you can introduce them to your brand through a professional company profile, which is shared with attendees in advance of the event. The €1,300 participation fee includes an exhibit space for your booth (3 meters by 2 meters), distribution of your company profile to all registered students, the option to share a pre-event video message, and featured logo placement on the official event website . Digital Career Days Our virtual recruitment fairs are hosted via Zoom and feature up to eight companies in a streamlined, two-hour session. Typically attracting around 70 participants, each event kicks off with a series of five-minute company pitches, followed by dedicated breakout rooms for interactive Q&A. This format allows your team to share links and resources through the chat while engaging directly with students via live video or text-based questions, fostering meaningful professional connections. The €1,300 fee covers participation in the high-visibility company pitch session, a dedicated breakout room for targeted Q&A, featured company and contact information on our recruitment platform, and logo placement on the official event event website . Company Presentations In addition to our Career Day series, the Career Center offers tailored opportunities for individual company presentations . These sessions can be hosted either on-campus or virtually, providing a flexible platform to showcase your organization’s culture and specific career opportunities. Company Contact Fair The RWTH Career Center partners with the student initiative bonding to organize the annual bonding Company Contact Fair each November. This well-established event offers a proven platform for connecting students and employers. For more information, please visit the bonding website . If you have any questions, please contact the bonding team directly at ac_messe@bonding.de . Footer Services Contact and Directions Legal Notice Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement Site Map Safety Feedback Glossary of Academic Terms Other Portals RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle RWTH Jobs Portal University Library Athletics and Recreation Intranet RWTH in Simple English Further Institutions © 2026 RWTH Aachen University Social Media Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Facebook Threads BlueSky Mastodon RWTH Social Media"
    },
