th Portal Career Submenu: Career RWTH Jobs Portal Working at RWTH Working in RWTH’s Scientific Community Working in Management, Administration, Technology & IT Career & Personal Development RWTH Welcome Center Interesting Facts Living in Aachen and Beyond Sustainability Submenu: Sustainability Sustainability Strategy Sustainability Report Sustainability Mission Statement Sustainability Focus Areas Networks Help Build a Sustainable RWTH Newsletter, FAQ and Downloads Faculties Submenu: Faculties Faculty 1 Mathematics and Natural Sciences Faculty 2 Architecture Faculty 3 Civil Engineering Faculty 4 Mechanical Engineering Faculty 5 Georesources and Materials Engineering Faculty 6 Electrical Engineering and Information Technology Faculty 7 Arts and Humanities Faculty 8 Business and Economics Faculty 9 Computer Science Faculty 10 Medicine Information for... Quick Access Prospective Students First Year Students Students Early-Career Researchers Researchers International Alumni School Students Corporate Visitors Press Tools RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle Intranet Services Dining Hall Menus RWTH Navigator Student Resources and Support Official Announcements Institutions University Library IT Center Center for Teaching and Learning Services Athletics and Recreation Central University Administration Search by Name Search for Search You Are Here: Start About RWTH Featured RWTH Events Honors Awarded to Our Graduates and Early-Career Researchers Honors Awarded to Our Graduates and Early-Career Researchers Borchers’ Medal Springorum Commemorative Coin Friedrich Wilhelm Prize Contact Central University Administration Division 3.2 – Events and RWTHextern Citizens' Forum Work Send Email RWTH celebrates its graduates with an annual Graduation Celebration held in the dressage stadium of the Aachen-Laurensberger Rennverein. Around 5,000 people take part in this cross-faculty ceremony every year and enjoy the graduates' memorable entry into the dressage stadium, their recognition by the Rector and Chancellor of RWTH, by professors of the University, and by a keynote speech given by the current winner of the Aachen Engineering Award. Finally, the event finishes with a particular highlight, when around 1,500 graduates hurl their caps into the Aachen sky. In addition, the best doctorates are honored with the Borchers' Plaque , the Springorum Memorial Coin is awarded for the best final theses, and the Friedrich Wilhelm Prize promotes research and teaching. Similar Topics Awards and Honors Footer Services Contact and Directions Legal Notice Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement Site Map Safety Feedback Glossary of Academic Terms Other Portals RWTHonline RWTHcontacts RWTHmoodle RWTH Jobs Portal University Library Athletics and Recreation Intranet RWTH in Simple English Further Institutions © 2026 RWTH Aachen University Social Media Instagram LinkedIn YouTube TikTok Facebook Threads BlueSky Mastodon RWTH Social Media"
